# The wanderers, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): each role's "Need a
# hand?" (slot 2, the wanderers' asks) comes out of their own trouble, told their way. Not while
# they're bitten (slot 2 is the antidote then). The road's news is theirs too, and not all of it is
# true. Voice: plain, each person their own. Lines are spoken straight to the player.

# A first meeting: who they are and what they do on the roads (the built memory: met once you've
# dealt with them). Greet lines are conditional: the talk screen shows only a line that says something.
conv wanderer.intro
for wanderer
when !wbitten
greet
prio world
once
voice plain

node start
  say? !met & role:trader :: "You look like a customer. I'm a trader: I walk the roads between the towns with a pack of what people need, and swap it for what they've got. Tins, mostly."
  say? !met & role:doctor :: "Don't mind me, I'm only looking at your colour. I was a doctor at the hospital before the line closed. Now I walk the roads with one bag and see whoever needs seeing."
  say? !met & role:scavenger :: "Easy. I'm not after anything you've got. I pick through the empty towns for what's left and swap it on. Somebody has to, or it all just rots on the shelves."
  say? !met & role:deserter :: "Don't come closer. Please. I wore Bastion's badge once. Now I'm nobody, walking. If anyone in green asks, you never saw me, and I'll do the same for you."
  say? !met & role:preacher :: "Peace on you, whoever you are. I carry the bells from town to town and ring them so the lonely know somebody's still here. I'm not much of a priest. I'm what's left."
  say? !met & role:courier :: "I carry letters between the houses and the towns, for anyone who still writes. Half the addresses are gone. I deliver them anyway, to whoever's nearest."
  say? !met & role:mechanic :: "Hold on, let me wipe my hands. I fix what still runs. Engines don't care about the line. Give me a part and some fuel and I'll get most things going."
  say? !met & role:kid :: "I'm not supposed to talk to people I don't know. You look all right, though. Do you know where the houses with the bears on the doors are?"

conv wanderer.trader.trouble
for wanderer:trader
when !wbitten
topic "How's trade been?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say? outbreak:overrun :: "Slow. Nobody walks to market when the market might eat them. Half the towns I used to stop in are theirs now, and the other half have bolted their doors to me."
  say? need:food :: "Everybody wants food, and nobody's got anything to swap for it but stories. I don't eat stories. I've tried. They're very filling for about an hour."
  say? rain :: "Wet. Wet stock is cheap stock. I'm selling damp bandages at a very fair price. Damp matches at a fairer one. Nobody wants the matches."
  say "Up and down. Mostly down. I carry what one town has too much of to the town that's short of it. When the roads are shut, I'm just a person with a heavy bag."
  > @why "What's holding it up?" -> hold
  > @cut "And if I helped? What's my cut?" -> cut
  > @hand "Do you need a hand with anything?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @no "Good luck with it." -> hub

node hold
  say "Roads. Tolls. People. Mostly people. The Red Hand wants a tin a car at every crossroads, Bastion wants to search the bag, and the sick want the person carrying it."
  say "Somebody always wants the thing you're carrying more than you do. I've a few deals half done that need another pair of legs. I'd pay what I could."
  > @hand1 "Then tell me what you need doing." -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node cut
  say "Your cut is my gratitude and a better price next time. My gratitude is very sincere. My prices are less so. And the houses hear who helped who. That's worth more than either."
  > @hand2 "Fair enough. What do you need?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.doctor.trouble
for wanderer:doctor
when !wbitten
topic "Who are you worried about?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say? dusk :: "Whoever's still out after dark. It's nearly dark. So, everyone. The bites people get at dusk are the ones I hear about at dawn, too late to do anything."
  say? outbreak:collapse :: "Everybody with a scratch who's telling themselves it's a fence. I've seen four this week. Two of them told me in time."
  say? symptoms :: "You, mostly. You're grey and you're sweating in the cold. Sit down. No, really. Sit, and let me look at you before we talk about anyone else."
  say "The ones who won't come to me. They're always the ones who should. Half my work now is walking to people who've decided they're fine, and finding out they're not."
  > @who "Anyone in particular?" -> who
  > @nurse "Let me sort your bag for you." -> kit   if bg:nurse,doctor
  > @hand "Can I help you with them?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @no "Take care of yourself." -> hub

node who
  say "A family on the farm road with a child who coughs. A man who won't let anyone see his leg. And somebody bitten in the next town, holed up, waiting for a dressing I can't walk there before dark."
  say "Ordinary things kill more people than the sick do now. They're just slower about it. If you've legs and a bit of nerve, I've work for both."
  > @hand1 "I've got legs. What do you need?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node kit
  say "You know what you're looking at. Good. Half of this is out of date. The other half I'm pretending isn't. The antiseptic's gone, so I clean with what the Red Hand sells as vodka."
  > @hand2 "Then let me help you. What's needed?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.scavenger.trouble
for wanderer:scavenger
when !wbitten
topic "What are you after out here?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say? town:looted :: "Anything nobody's taken. Round here that's a short list. This town's been picked to the bone. Somebody even took the light bulbs, and there's no power to put them in."
  say? night :: "Sleep. But since you're asking, batteries. Torches, radios, anything that eats them. A battery's worth two tins now, and three after dark."
  say "Whatever's left. Whatever's worth a tin. Same thing, these days. I go into the empty towns in daylight and come out before the sick wake up. That's the whole trick."
  > @where "Where's worth looking?" -> where
  > @hand "Need a hand with anything?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @no "Happy hunting." -> hub

node where
  say "If I told you, it'd be worth less. That's how this works: knowing where is the only thing I've got that doesn't weigh anything."
  say "Help me with something first and I'll think about telling you. I've a job or two that's easier with two. You'd get a share and a friend on the road."
  > @hand1 "All right. What's the job?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.deserter.trouble
for wanderer:deserter
when !wbitten
topic "Is someone following you?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say? kit:other :: "Maybe. You're wearing colours. Whose? Never mind. Don't stand so close. Last time someone in colours stood that close to me, it was to read me my name."
  say? feud:bastion :: "By Bastion? They've a feud to fight and a line to hold. They've enough to do. They'd still make time for me. They make time for everyone who walked."
  say "Always. Or I think so, which is the same thing when you're trying to sleep. I left Bastion without asking, and Bastion doesn't forget a name on its roster."
  > @why "Who'd come after you?" -> who
  > @soldier "You left your post. That counts." -> post   if bg:soldier,police
  > @hand "Need a hand with anything?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @no "Keep moving, then." -> hub

node who
  say "People I used to stand next to. Men from my section. They'd say they're looking for me to bring me home. They'd mean it kindly. That's worse."
  say "Meanwhile I've got to eat, and there's things on the road I can't do without being seen. If you'd do them for me, I'd make it worth your while."
  > @hand1 "What is it you need doing?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node post
  say "It does. I know. I still hear the roll some nights, from a long way off. My name's on the board as missing. That's the kind word for it. There are other words."
  > @hand2 "Even so. Do you need a hand?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.preacher.trouble
for wanderer:preacher
when !wbitten
topic "What are you praying for?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say? epilogue :: "That the road out is a road out, and not another checkpoint with a loudspeaker. I've stopped praying for big things. I'm saving my breath for the walk."
  say? cure>=75 :: "For the lab up the hill, and the cure they keep saying is close. Don't tell anyone. I'd lose my reputation for not trusting anything with a clipboard."
  say? outbreak:overrun :: "For quiet. The bells were for company. They brought the wrong company. I ring them softer now, and only by day."
  say "For whoever needs it. You can have one if you like. Free. It's the only free thing left in the Zone. Even the Red Hand hasn't found a way to toll a prayer."
  > @bells "Why do you carry the bells?" -> bells
  > @hand "Can I do anything for you?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @no "Pray for me, then." -> hub

node bells
  say "So the lonely ones know someone's here. People shut in their houses since Day 1 hear the bell and come to the window. Some come down. That's my whole ministry now."
  say "The sick hear it too, and come. Everything has a cost now. Even comfort. So I ring and walk on, and sometimes I need somebody to do what I can't."
  > @hand1 "What is it you can't do?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

conv wanderer.courier.trouble
for wanderer:courier
when !wbitten
topic "Whose letters are running late?"
prio ask
voice plain

node start
  say? outbreak:overrun :: "Everyone's. The roads are theirs now, most of them. I go round. Round takes days, and a letter that takes days to cross a valley isn't much of a letter."
  say? edge :: "There's one in my bag for someone outside the line. I carry it anyway. One day there'll be an outside again, and I want to be the first one there with the post."
  say "A mother in one town has written to her son in another. Neither knows the other's alive. I'm the only one in the Zone who knows both, and I can't get there."
  > @why "Why can't you deliver them?" -> why
  > @hand "Can I help you get them there?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @no "Safe roads." -> hub

node why
  say "Because one of the towns is a bad town now, thick with the sick. I'd go. I'm a coward, not an idiot. Mostly a coward."
  say "Somebody with a steadier nerve could get a letter there and back by dark. I'd pay in what I've got, and I'd owe you, and I always pay what I owe."
  > @hand1 "I'll carry it. What do I need to do?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

# The road's news. A wanderer's version of a burned town has the Red Hand in it, which the Red Hand
# denies with the truth (~truth:gossip.burned@burned, their leaders and people).
conv wanderer.road.news
for wanderer:trader, wanderer:scavenger, wanderer:deserter, wanderer:preacher, wanderer:courier, wanderer:doctor
topic "What did you pass on the road?"
prio world
voice plain

bind burned = news:burned
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by
bind from = news:taken_from
bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind at = news:leader_dead_at
bind horde = news:horde
bind truck = news:truck
bind bit = news:bite

node start
  jump news:burned -> burned
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:taken -> taken
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:truck -> truck
  jump news:bite -> bite
  say? epilogue :: "Queues at the road checkpoints. People in their good coats, holding suitcases, waiting for a loudspeaker to say their name. Processing, they call it."
  say? edge :: "Drones. Close to the line, there's always one up. It hums like it's thinking about you. I keep my hands where it can see them and my feet off the verge."
  say? stage:fever :: "You, looking like that. You're grey. Sit down a minute before you fall down, and tell me if it's a bite or a fever, because it matters which."
  say "Nothing much. Empty cars with the doors open. A suitcase in a ditch. There's always a shoe in the road. I've stopped wondering where the other one went."
  > @back0 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node burned
  say "{bind:burned}, burning. Black smoke you could see for miles. The Red Hand's work, I'd say. I saw one of their lorries on the road after, going the other way, fast." ~lie:gossip.burned@burned
  > @catch "The Red Hand say burning is waste." -> caught   callout gossip.burned@burned
  > @back1 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node caught
  say "Do they. Well. It was a lorry, on a road, near a fire. I might have filled in the rest myself. People like a story with someone to blame in it, me included."
  > @back2 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node dead
  say "{bind:dead} is dead, at {bind:at}. One of the people in charge. I heard it three ways on the road. Two of them were sad about it. The third was buying drinks."
  > @back3 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node taken
  say "{bind:who} put their flag up at {bind:took}. {bind:from} took theirs down and went. I watched the pole change from the hill. Nobody's flag ever stopped the sick."
  > @back4 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node horde
  say "A crowd of the sick near {bind:horde}, following some noise. Hundreds, shuffling the same way. I went round. Round is my favourite direction."
  > @back5 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node truck
  say "A supply truck that didn't get where it was going. {bind:truck}. Doors open, nobody in the cab. I didn't look in the back. I've learned not to look in the back."
  > @back6 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub

node bite
  say "Somebody got bitten near {bind:bit}. I saw the blood on the road and the person walk on. Brave, or not thinking yet. Thinking comes later, with the fever."
  > @back7 "Let me ask you something else." -> hub
